# House Adel — Cloudflare Pages routing.
#
# One rule, and it is the one a single-page application cannot launch without.
# Every route on this site is a real address that can be typed, bookmarked,
# refreshed and shared — /work, /contact, /marvell-20, /privacy, /terms — but
# only /index.html exists on disk. Without this, a refresh on any of them is a
# hard 404 from the edge before a single line of the application runs.
#
# 200, not 302: the address stays exactly as the visitor typed it, and the
# router reads it from location on the way in. A redirect would rewrite the
# address bar to / and lose the page they asked for.
#
# Assets are matched by the file system first, so this rule never shadows them.
/*    /index.html   200
